WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.202
-Here at "The Tonight Show,"
we love songs,

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:05.705
and we especially love songs
written by our audience members

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:06.973
in under an hour.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.274
That's right.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.709
It's time for "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.743
Here we go.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:11.977
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.977 --> 00:00:14.681
-♪ Something song,
and I'm singing a song ♪

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:18.851
♪ And I'm writing a song
about another song ♪

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.052
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:22.655
Welcome to "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.958
Before the show, we went through
our great audience,

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.692
our lovely audience,
and we picked out two people

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:29.228
who said they were musicians.

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:30.396
We don't know if they are.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.898
But we gave them each
a made-up song title

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:34.200
and gave them an hour

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.936
to write an original song
based on that title.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.206
Here's a shot of them practicing
backstage minutes ago.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.407
There you go.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:42.575
I can't wait to see
what they came up with,

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.576
so let's meet them right now.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:44.977
Come on over, guys.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:46.546
Welcome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.947
Nice to see you.
♪♪

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:48.982
Nice to see you.
Welcome to the show.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.549
Welcome to the show.
How are you?

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.386
-Good.
-Alright, here we go.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.687
Contestant number 1,
what is your name,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.988
and where are you from?

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:58.458
-My name's Marcia Belsky,
and I'm from Brooklyn, New York.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.726
-Yeah, Brooklyn!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:03.062
Come on! Marcia Belsky.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.465
Marcia, what was the title
that was given to you?

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.067
-It was "Scrolling Through
TikTok on Thanksgiving Day."

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.335
-Yeah, that's right.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.871
I feel like a lot of people
will be doing that.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.574
"Scrolling Through TikTok
on Thanksgiving Day."

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.942
What instrument
will you be playing?

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.010
-I'm doing piano.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.311
-Oh, I love the piano.
Alright, good.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.779
Alright, why don't you go over
and get ready,

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.915
get inspired, get set,
and get ready to hear...

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:26.519
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.588
And now, ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.055
here to perform
the world premiere of

00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:31.458
the soon-to-be classic

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:34.527
"Scrollin' TikTok
on Thanksgiving Day,"

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.928
it's Marcia Belsky.

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:37.964
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:46.539
-♪ Last year this time, I was so
lonely at the holidays ♪

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:49.208
♪ But this year,
I'll be sitting right across

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.743
from everyone I love ♪

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:54.780
♪ As I scroll TikTok
on Thanksgiving Day ♪

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.483
♪ Scrollin' TikTok
on Thanksgiving Day ♪

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.685
♪ Watching couples
who hate each other

00:01:59.685 --> 00:02:01.554
pull dangerous pranks like ♪

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:05.725
♪ Watch me scare
my pregnant wife, okay ♪

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.427
♪ Now your baby's on its way ♪

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:10.996
♪ Scrollin' TikTok
on Thanksgiving Day ♪

00:02:10.996 --> 00:02:12.698
♪ A 12-year-old tarot reader

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:15.268
said love's coming my way ♪

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:22.041
♪ I'm in community here with
the tweens on TikTok, baby ♪

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.677
♪ Scrollin' TikTok
on Thanksgiving Day ♪

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:29.882
♪ I'm so thankful for my phone ♪

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:34.287
♪ And I guess also my family ♪

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.889
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:40.126
-That's great.
"And I guess also my family."

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.827
Marcia Belsky!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:45.431
Hey, that was incredible!
Come on over, Marcia.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.434
Yeah, "I'm so thankful for
my phone.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.769
Oh, yeah, and also my family."

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.138
Yeah. Alright, let's meet
contestant number 2.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.739
What is your name?
And where are you from?

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:55.842
-My name is Brooks Allison.
I'm from Brooklyn, as well.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.844
-Hey, Brooklyn
in the house tonight!

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:00.779
-Mm-hmm.
-Brooks Allison.

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:04.750
Brooks, what is the song title
we gave you this evening?

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.854
-"Stuck in an Elevator with
Ed Sheeran."

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.888
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:11.924
-It's very possible.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:13.659
-It probably did happen,
you know?

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:16.796
Elevators are kind of an
old technology, but, I mean,

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.732
I'm sure that even Ed Sheeran
uses an elevator, yeah.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.133
-Sure.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.936
-And he probably got stuck maybe
once or twice with someone.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:28.240
And I probably would enjoy being
stuck in an elevator.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.875
But what instrument will you
be playing?

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:31.878
-I'll be playing guitar.
-You'll be playing guitar?

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.246
Okay.
Why don't you get over there.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.814
-Thank you.
-Get in the zone.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:35.915
Come over here, Marcia.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.049
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.351
That was great, by the way.
-Thank you.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:45.858
-Ladies and gentlemen, get ready
for the world premiere of

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:49.662
"Stuck in an Elevator with
Ed Sheeran" by Brooks Allison!

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.763
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:00.473
-♪ I got in an elevator and was
headed for the sixth floor ♪

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:08.381
♪ There was a big crash,
and the elevator works no more ♪

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:09.782
[ Imitates crash ]

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.251
♪ I started to panic,
turned around,

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.888
there was a red-headed man ♪

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:22.661
♪ Little did I know that I
was stuck in an elevator with ♪

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:24.063
♪ Ed Sheeran ♪

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:28.835
♪ He told me I
looked perfect tonight ♪

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.936
♪ I said, "Now's not the time" ♪

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:33.706
♪ He said,
"No, that's just a line

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:36.309
from one of my songs called
'Perfect'" ♪

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.310
♪ I said,
"Yeah, I know the song ♪

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.213
♪ I hear it all the time ♪

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.847
♪ Especially while driving ♪

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:45.484
♪ But right now, all I care
about is surviving this

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:48.721
elevator thing ♪

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.523
♪ He said,
"Yeah, that was dumb" ♪

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.358
♪ I said,
"Don't worry about it" ♪

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.794
♪ And the doors opened up ♪

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:58.430
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.833
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my gosh.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:04.770
Give it up for Brooks Allison
right there.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.738
[ Cheers and applause ]
That was awesome.

00:05:06.738 --> 00:05:10.476
Brooks, come on over.
♪♪

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:13.179
Thank you, Brooks.
Wow!

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.814
It seemed like
it really happened, almost.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.883
Alright, now it's time
to see who won,

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:21.353
so we're going to let our great
audience decide the winner.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.923
Was it Marcia Belsky?
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.258
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:29.362
Or was it Brooks Allison?

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.330
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.733
It looks like the winner is
Brooks Allison!

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:35.601
[ Dinging ]
♪♪

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:40.606
Brooks, you're going to be going
home with $1,000

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.709
and a "Tonight Show" notebook
for writing more songs.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.111
-Thank you, thank you,
thank you.

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.144
-Congratulations.
That was a great job.

00:05:46.144 --> 00:05:49.515
-Thank you, thank you.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.083
-But no one goes home
empty-handed.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.985
Our other contestant tonight
will also receive

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.520
a notebook and $1,000.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.455
-Ooh!

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:57.723
-Thank you for being here.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.258
Give it up for your
two new instant songwriters.

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:00.360
[ Cheers and applause ]

